Question: can reusable extraction recover selected typed readings, explicitly
account for all 23 notes, and check the declared statement/note bridges?
Pass requires source bindings, supported context, exact arithmetic or explicit
rounding compatibility, 23 bounded note dispositions, and adversarial rejection
tests. Hash/anchor failures, missing/duplicate required notes, ambiguous required
readings, invalid contexts and failed arithmetic veto the implementation until
repaired. External-access failures block only their dependent incorporation or
version claims. Counts and reconciliations cannot establish semantic completion,
accounting compliance, forecast validity or human acceptance.

The expected failure modes are copied constants, mixed extraction offsets,
wrong scale/sign/date, cash-perimeter substitution, fair value or notional
substitution for carrying value, and overlapping revenue partitions. These are
repair triggers and deterministic test targets. A successful build without these
checks would not answer the question. No statistical comparison, research run,
performance ranking or numerical default promotion is planned; a tuned baseline
ladder and random seeds are inapplicable. Stop for corrupted required inputs or
unsupported mandatory extraction; preserve specific external residuals and
continue independent work. Only the two declared files are written under the
master deliverable directory.

